---
// Member portal landing.
//
// MVP: the portal is gated by an opaque session token (magic link)
// which we will wire up in a follow-up. For Phase 3, this page
// explains what the portal will be and how to request access.
//
// See MASTER_SPEC §12.4 (member auth).
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Member portal"
  description="Sign in to manage your membership, preferences, and memory."
  canonicalPath="/portal/"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Member portal</h1>
      <p>
        The portal is the place where you see and manage your membership. You can edit preferences,
        mark facts as do-not-mention, view your timeline, and export a copy of your data.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sign in is by magic link. We do not use passwords. We do not require you to keep any session
        longer than you want. We do not invent facts about you.
      </p>
      <h2>What you can do here</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>See <strong>what the Society remembers about you</strong> and edit or remove it.</li>
        <li>Update your contact details, postal address, and chapter.</li>
        <li>Choose which optional services are on (newsletter, post, gifts, calls, etc.).</li>
        <li>Request a manufactured commitment scenario.</li>
        <li>Request an appearance service quote.</li>
        <li>Export a copy of your data.</li>
        <li>Cancel at any time.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The portal is not yet open. The current waiting list is separate and does not create paid
        membership.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/waiting-list/" class="hero__cta">Join the waiting list</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
